{"labs": [{"stimuli": [{"id": 0, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "_data": []}, {"id": 1, "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe7n2le03ob04re2aud01", "coverimg": "enpe7n2le03ob04re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"id": 0, "image": "enpe7n2le03ob04re2img01.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Kyle</span>: Hey, Mandy. There is something I need to summarize for my class workshop. Can you help me? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mandy</span>: Sure, Kyle. I guess it's related to software. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Kyle</span>: Yes, it is! I need to describe modeling languages and talk about them. I watched a documentary and it showed the origin of modeling languages. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mandy</span>: Ok, tell me about the documentary so I have a better idea of what you need.", "time": "0"}, {"id": 1, "image": "enpe7n2le03ob04re2img02.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Kyle</span>: Well, I know that modern software projects are complex, in other words, a software is not a program itself but a series of systems or modules. Because they are so large, there are easier ways to design those software projects. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mandy</span>: That's right! And that's when programmers modeled software projects using modeling languages. With them, it is possible to map out the structure of those programs like the components and the relationships they hold. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Kyle</span>: Oh, I see! There are significant software projects that use the modeling languages to make their creation easier. I understand that the Universal Modeling Language is the most used in programming.", "time": "26000"}, {"id": 2, "image": "enpe7n2le03ob04re2img03.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Mandy</span>: Exactly! It is the fastest and easiest way to shape the structure of a program. It describes software in three ways: functions seen by the user; objects, attributes, and relationships; and system behavior. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Kyle</span>: Ok, I guess it's necessary to use a modeling language to structure a software before people code the program, right? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mandy</span>: That's right! That's how programmers interact easier with programs. It makes creation easier. Just take into account that UML uses a variety of diagrams to shape different processes.", "time": "71000"}]}, "type": "slideshow"}], "_data": []}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "type": "WLC", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can talk about modeling languages.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can exchange information about modeling languages.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can give examples of modeling languages and talk briefly about them.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "How do you think programmers create software?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Do you think that the software programs we use today are different from the ones we used 10 years ago? What changed?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "How to Build Software", "type": "free_type_text_area"}]}, {"id": 1, "type": "STI", "stimuli_ids": [1], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"id": 0, "responses": [{"selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, {"selected": 0, "id": 1, "correct": 1, "_data": 