"target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about modeling languages.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Understand key information about the concepts, principles, and methodologies in simple spoken and written situations.  Talk about programming techniques, use cases, kinds, and sequences in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures.  Identifies general aspects related to Software Programming in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n2le03ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Look for more information about modeling languages.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Describe your opinion about modeling languages.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write on your notebook 3 functions of modeling languages and share it with your teacher.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I look for more information about modeling languages.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I describe modeling languages.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write on my notebook 3 functions of modeling languages and share it with your teacher.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "summarize \t\t", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to express an idea in a shorter and more synthetized way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There is something I need to summarize for my class workshop.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le03ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "be related to \t\t", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to have a connection or be linked to something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I guess it's related to software.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le03ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "series \t\t", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a number of things that share characteristics", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A software is not a program itself but a series of systems or modules.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le03ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "map out \t\t", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to plan or design something with detail", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(phrasal verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: With them, it is possible to map out the structure of those programs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le03ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "significant \t\t", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a representative quantity ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are significant software projects that use the modeling languages to make their creation easier.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le03ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "shape \t\t", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to give form ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It is the fastest and easiest way to shape the structure of a program.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le03ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Adjectives and Nouns to Talk about Modeling Languages", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are many words that people use to talk about specific or more specialized topics. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When talking about modeling languages, we can use some words that are special to this topic.<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Nouns</span> like <strong>software</strong>, <strong>systems</strong>, <strong>modules</strong>, are characteristic when talking about computers and related things.<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Adjectives</span> like <strong>significant</strong>, <strong>modern</strong>,<strong> large</strong>, or <strong>complex</strong>, give attributes to those nouns. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I know that modern software projects are complex.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Because they are so large, there are easier ways to design those software projects. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There are significant software projects that use the modeling languages to make their creation easier. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Action Verbs in Simple Present and Simple Past to Talk Modeling Languages", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Action verbs</span> talk about actions people perform.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Action verbs</span> describe a wide variety of actions people perform every day. In this case, there are some action verbs we can use to talk about modeling languages.<br/><br/>  Verbs like <strong>model</strong>, <strong>code</strong>, <strong>interact</strong>, <strong>summarize</strong>, <strong>describe</strong>, and <strong>show</strong>, have different meanings based on different contexts. However, if we talk about software and related topics, these verbs change their meaning. For example, the verb <strong>model</strong> changes its meaning if we talk about fashion.<br/><br/>  Those verbs can be used in present or in past. Because those are regular verbs, to use them in past you only need to add <strong>\u2013ed</strong> at the end of the verb.<br/><br/>  Let's take a look at the examples below. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "There is something I need to summarize for my class workshop. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I need to describe modeling languages and talk about them.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "That's right! And that's when programmers modeled software projects using modeling languages.", "type": "example"}]}]}